crates/puca-agent/refactor.cjs
frontend/fix_*.cjs
frontend/patch_*.cjs
frontend/src/update_*.cjs
# Unreferenced scratch: nothing declares `mod icon_test`.
frontend/src-tauri/src/icon_test.rs

# These were COMMITTED by an agent session on 2026-07-30 (1.8 GB of deploy
# tarballs plus the session-export/ Claude transcripts) and had to be rewritten
# out of the branch before it could be pushed. Never again.
/src.tar.gz
/src-tarball.tar.gz
/webapp-dist.tar.gz
/dist-tarball.tar.gz
/session-export*/
/session-export-*.zip
# OTA bundles. The prefix is per-deployment (MOBILE_BUNDLE_PREFIX in
# hosts.conf), and a deployment older than the rename still uses its
# original one — so match any prefix rather than the current product's.
frontend/*-web-*.zip
frontend/*-web-*.enc.zip

# Clips spike outputs (results JSON, captured mp4s) — never commit measurements
frontend/e2e/spike-clips/results/

# Operator infrastructure identity. These were TRACKED until 2026-08-20 and had
# to be removed when the repo went public: hosts.conf carried production IPs and
# root SSH targets, known_hosts pinned those same boxes by name. The .example
# templates beside them are what ships; your real copies stay local.
#
# The rule this encodes, since it was already written three lines up and got
# violated anyway: prod topology does not belong in git. That now includes
# server IPs, SSH targets, host keys and LAN layout, not just credentials.
deploy/ops/hosts.conf
deploy/ops/known_hosts
!deploy/ops/hosts.conf.example
!deploy/ops/known_hosts.example

# WITHHELD — the H-1 write-up, which is exploit-level detail.
#
# The original reason was that production had not yet received the fix, and
# publishing a working attack against a live unpatched deployment is not
# something a rename/relicense pass gets to decide on its own.
#
# THAT CONDITION IS NOW MET. Verified 2026-08-25 against both hosts, over each
# host's own loopback rather than from outside: both serve an identical webapp
# bundle carrying the H-1 fix (the attributed-wrapper refusal and rotate-away
# paths are present in the shipped JavaScript), and both report v0.8.114.
#
# So this is no longer a safety hold. It is now a publication decision: whether
# a 29 KB internal audit document belongs in a repository that has deliberately
# dropped its other internal audit documents for being working artefacts rather
# than product. The README states the finding, the fix, the file it lives in and
# the limitation it does NOT close, which is the part a reader actually needs.
#
# If it is published, scrub it first — it was written against the private
# deployment and cites it.
docs/AUDIT_2026-08-20.md

# Operator-internal handover / infra notes, dated variants. The existing
# rule below only caught the undated filename; HANDOVER_2026-07-25.md at
# repo root slipped through the same policy it was supposed to be covered
# by. Glob broadened rather than adding another one-off name.
HANDOVER_*.md

# Internal manual QA backlog — operationally useful, not reader-useful; a
# stale, version-pinned test checklist has no place in a public release.
/task.md

# Desktop updater endpoint for a REAL deployment. Merged over tauri.conf.json
# at build time by frontend/scripts/tauri-build.mjs. Untracked for the same
# reason as hosts.conf: it names a domain you control, and a public repo must
# not bake one deployment's update server into everybody's build.
frontend/src-tauri/tauri.release.json
!frontend/src-tauri/tauri.release.example.json

# Your real download page. The tracked index.html is a generic template naming
# example.com; dual-ship.sh prefers this file when it exists so a real release
# never publishes the placeholder domain to actual users.
deploy/download-site/index.local.html

# Internal QA/verification reports — working artefacts, not deliverables.
# They cite file:line for security-sensitive logic and read as findings even
# after the findings are fixed.
/RENAME_VERIFICATION_*.md
/AUDIT_*.md

# Operator-internal working documents. These are process artefacts, not product:
# dated audits with UNFIXED findings still listed, remediation/agent-orchestration
# plans naming branches and commits that do not exist in this repository, a
# session handoff, and runbooks describing one particular machine and home
# uplink. A self-hoster needs none of them, and two of them are a to-do list for
# an attacker — the same reason docs/AUDIT_2026-08-20.md is held back above.
# Nothing in the tree links to any of them.
docs/AUDIT_2026-07-24.md
docs/AUDIT_2026-07-24_STATUS.md
# Retired for the launch: FEATURES.md was a 2025-12 manual QA audit ("Not
# tested"/"Broken" rows, an internal fix list) and AUTO_UPDATER_GUIDE.md
# described a CURRENT_VERSION constant, a get_platform_info() and a plain-zip
# OTA that no longer exist. Deleted from the tree; listed so they cannot
# drift back in from a stale checkout.
docs/FEATURES.md
docs/AUTO_UPDATER_GUIDE.md
docs/SETTINGS_AUDIT_2026-07-26.md
docs/REMEDIATION_PLAN.md
docs/SECURITY-REMAINING-2026-08-10.md
docs/DEVICES_HANDOFF.md
docs/TESTING_AND_LAUNCH.md
docs/VPS_MIGRATION.md
docs/SCREENSHARE_REDESIGN_PLAN.md

# screenshots and evidence from on-demand e2e harnesses (csp-smoke-desktop etc.)
frontend/e2e-artifacts/

# Written by the release step for GET /source (build.rs embeds it); never committed.
SOURCE_COMMIT
